    "short_description": "The Teachers Service Commission (TSC) of Kenya is an independent constitutional body established to manage human resources in the education sector. It is responsible for registering, recruiting, employing, assigning, promoting, disciplining, and terminating teachers in public schools and institutions. The TSC was formally established in 1967 and operates under various legislations, including the TSC Act 2012 and the Basic Education Act.\n\nHeadquartered in Nairobi, TSC has offices across all 47 counties. Its core mandate includes formulating policies, ensuring teaching standards, managing payroll, and facilitating career progression for teachers. The commission also plays a vital role in reviewing education and training standards, assessing teacher demand, and coordinating in-service training. TSC offers digital services through its online portal, including tools for payslip management, performance appraisal, and teacher assignment tracking.",
